  "summary": "I added a \"Close portal\" button below the canvas in src/main.ts. Typecheck and `validate` pass, and the render shows the portal open with the button under the canvas. I couldn't click the button in the render tool, so closing and reopening haven't been exercised in a browser.\n\nClicking the button toggles the portal. When closed, the vortex disc, the glow discs, the platform pool, the back haze, all particles and the three portal lights are hidden, so the stones and platform lose their colored light. `window.__TASK_STATE__` shows `portalActive: false` and `particleCount: 0`, and the label reads \"Open portal\". Clicking again shows everything and respawns the particles across their lifetimes, and the label returns to \"Close portal\". While closed, the particle simulation stops updating, and the ring, runes and camera sway keep animating."
